  "generated_model": "##### Sets and Parameters\n\nLet the day be divided into 48 half-hour intervals, indexed by $t = 1, 2, ..., 48$, corresponding to the following time slots and required waitstaff:\n\n| $t$ | Time                   | Requirement $r_t$ |\n|-----|------------------------|-------------------|\n| 1   | 2:00am - 2:30am        | 2                 |\n| 2   | 2:30am - 3:00am        | 3                 |\n| 3   | 3:00am - 3:30am        | 4                 |\n| 4   | 3:30am - 4:00am        | 6                 |\n| 5   | 4:00am - 4:30am        | 5                 |\n| 6   | 4:30am - 5:00am        | 4                 |\n| 7   | 5:00am - 5:30am        | 5                 |\n| 8   | 5:30am - 6:00am        | 6                 |\n| 9   | 6:00am - 6:30am        | 7                 |\n| 10  | 6:30am - 7:00am        | 8                 |\n| 11  | 7:00am - 7:30am        | 9                 |\n| 12  | 7:30am - 8:00am        | 9                 |\n| 13  | 8:00am - 8:30am        | 8                 |\n| 14  | 8:30am - 9:00am        | 8                 |\n| 15  | 9:00am - 9:30am        | 9                 |\n| 16  | 9:30am - 10:00am       | 9                 |\n| 17  | 10:00am - 10:30am      | 10                |\n| 18  | 10:30am - 11:00am      | 12                |\n| 19  | 11:00am - 11:30am      | 11                |\n| 20  | 11:30am - 12:00pm      | 11                |\n| 21  | 12:00pm - 12:30pm      | 12                |\n| 22  | 12:30pm - 1:00pm       | 11                |\n| 23  | 1:00pm - 1:30pm        | 10                |\n| 24  | 1:30pm - 2:00pm        | 9                 |\n| 25  | 2:00pm - 2:30pm        | 8                 |\n| 26  | 2:30pm - 3:00pm        | 7                 |\n| 27  | 3:00pm - 3:30pm        | 6                 |\n| 28  | 3:30pm - 4:00pm        | 5                 |\n| 29  | 4:00pm - 4:30pm        | 5                 |\n| 30  | 4:30pm - 5:00pm        | 6                 |\n| 31  | 5:00pm - 5:30pm        | 7                 |\n| 32  | 5:30pm - 6:00pm        | 8                 |\n| 33  | 6:00pm - 6:30pm        | 9                 |\n| 34  | 6:30pm - 7:00pm        | 10                |\n| 35  | 7:00pm - 7:30pm        | 9                 |\n| 36  | 7:30pm - 8:00pm        | 8                 |\n| 37  | 8:00pm - 8:30pm        | 7                 |\n| 38  | 8:30pm - 9:00pm        | 6                 |\n| 39  | 9:00pm - 9:30pm        | 5                 |\n| 40  | 9:30pm - 10:00pm       | 4                 |\n| 41  | 10:00pm - 10:30pm      | 4                 |\n| 42  | 10:30pm - 11:00pm      | 3                 |\n| 43  | 11:00pm - 11:30pm      | 3                 |\n| 44  | 11:30pm - 12:00am      | 3                 |\n| 45  | 12:00am - 12:30am      | 3                 |\n| 46  | 12:30am - 1:00am       | 4                 |\n| 47  | 1:00am - 1:30am        | 4                 |\n| 48  | 1:30am - 2:00am        | 4                 |\n\nLet $r_t$ denote the required number of waitstaff for time slot $t$.\n\n##### Decision Variables\n\nLet $x_s$ be the number of waitstaff whose shift starts at time slot $s$, for $s = 1, 2, ..., 48$.\n\nEach shift covers 8 consecutive hours = 16 consecutive half-hour slots. For each $s$, a shift starting at slot $s$ covers slots $s, s+1, ..., s+15$ (modulo 48, i.e., wrapping around midnight).\n\n##### Objective Function\n\n$\\min \\sum_{s=1}^{48} x_s$\n\n##### Constraints\n\nFor each time slot $t = 1, 2, ..., 48$:\n\n$\\sum_{k=0}^{15} x_{(t - k - 1 \\mod 48) + 1} \\geq r_t$\n\nwhere $x_{(t - k - 1 \\mod 48) + 1}$ is the number of waitstaff whose shift started $k$ half-hours before slot $t$ (with wrap-around).\n\n##### Variable Domains\n\n$x_s \\in \\mathbb{Z}_{\\geq 0}$, for all $s = 1, ..., 48$\n\n##### Retrieved Information\n\n{\n  \"time_slots\": [\n    \"2:00am - 2:30am\",\n    \"2:30am - 3:00am\",\n    \"3:00am - 3:30am\",\n    \"3:30am - 4:00am\",\n    \"4:00am - 4:30am\",\n    \"4:30am - 5:00am\",\n    \"5:00am - 5:30am\",\n    \"5:30am - 6:00am\",\n    \"6:00am - 6:30am\